  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A swimmer can swim with velocity of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> in still water. Water flowing in a river has velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>. The direction with respect to the direction of flow of river water he should swim in order to reach the point on the other bank just opposite to his starting point is ________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.&nbsp;</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer) (find the angle in degree)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "120",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt\"><img src=\"assets\\st0077_bea1819e6ebe.png\" style=\"width: 211px; height: 111px;\" /></p>"
  }
